gsnaugdesign:dd-0015
    a gsndesign:RetiredDecision ;
    gsndesign:retirementReason """Withdrawn at 0.2.0 together with gsnaug:TopSubjectContext and gsnaug:TopObjectContext. gsnaug:assures and gsnaug:requiredBy say the same thing directly and work for a case that draws no top-level context, which is the case the two classes were introduced to fall back from."""@en ;
    gsndesign:supersededBy gsnaugdesign:dd-0041 ;
    gsndesign:formalism gsndesign:OWL ;
    gsndesign:naturalLanguage "The two top-level contexts are subclasses of the GSN context, so a GSN-only tool treats them as ordinary contexts."@en ;
